  "decision_discriminator": "The action discriminator is target evidence, not species labels or donor count: P. putida has a native sugar-independent route and a documented failure of PtsN to replace fructose EIIA; Caulobacter separates its Ntr effectors from sugar permeases and its mannose assignments originate in an incorrect transporter EC mapping. E. coli has measured cross-system phosphate exchange in vitro but lacks demonstrated native sugar-uptake participation for the Ntr branch, so physiological process assignment is over-annotation rather than an absolute negative. Bona fide E. coli/Bacillus HPr controls retain the sugar process because they feed sugar-specific EIIA proteins in the native carbohydrate route; common ancestry at PTN002135312 does not erase this functional divergence.",
